WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.010 --> 00:00:07.687
- This is A$AP Ferg, and
I'mma teach you how to dougie.

00:00:07.687 --> 00:00:09.153
Nah, I'mma teach you how to ride the bike.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:14.233
- [Narrator] We caught up with A$AP Ferg,

00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:15.970
and he taught us some bike-riding basics,

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:17.930
as well as some advanced techniques.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:20.060
You'll notice that Ferg
isn't wearing a helmet,

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.130
but you definitely should.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.270
Like this guy.

00:00:23.270 --> 00:00:25.760
First up, let's talk seat height,

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.380
which is ideally at the hip.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:29.480
- First, y'all gotta make sure

00:00:29.480 --> 00:00:31.530
your seat is at the right height.

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:34.010
I like to wheelie, and
when my seat is too low,

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:36.050
I can't keep the bike up too long.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:37.160
I gotta keep it up a little higher

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.980
so I can just throw it up one more time.

00:00:38.980 --> 00:00:42.120
- [Narrator] Next up, brakes.
Because before you can ride,

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:44.808
you have to know how to stop.

00:00:44.808 --> 00:00:46.623
- These are the two brakes right here.

00:00:46.623 --> 00:00:49.040
You have a back brake, and
you have a front brake.

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:50.900
Front brake on the left.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.004
Back brake on the right.

00:00:53.004 --> 00:00:54.450
Make sure that they're nice and quick.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:56.000
You've got the adjuster right here,

00:00:57.020 --> 00:00:59.733
just in case it's a little loose.

00:01:00.840 --> 00:01:01.790
It works like this.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.710
- [Narrator] Gliding can help
you get a feel for balance.

00:01:06.710 --> 00:01:08.102
Here's how it's done.

00:01:08.102 --> 00:01:09.878
- I'mma start y'all off with something

00:01:09.878 --> 00:01:12.270
very simple, very easy.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:16.400
You take your left foot,
and you pedal down,

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:17.650
give yourself some motion,

00:01:19.990 --> 00:01:20.823
and push.

00:01:23.978 --> 00:01:26.010
- [Narrator] Now that
you've got balancing down,

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:27.763
it's time to pedal.

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:31.371
- I'mma teach you guys how to pedal now.

00:01:31.371 --> 00:01:32.866
It's not hard at all.

00:01:32.866 --> 00:01:34.099
You'll be like me.

00:01:46.695 --> 00:01:49.513
And then it's all about the flow.

00:01:51.920 --> 00:01:54.080
Don't be scared. Let it flow.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:56.490
You have to be fearless.
Don't be afraid to fall

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:58.703
off the bike a little bit sometimes.

00:02:00.901 --> 00:02:02.630
It's just the flow.

00:02:02.630 --> 00:02:05.137
- [Narrator] Once you're
confident in your basic skills,

00:02:05.137 --> 00:02:07.947
you can move on to
tricks, like the wheelie.

00:02:07.947 --> 00:02:09.440
- It has to be like this.

00:02:11.139 --> 00:02:13.158
And you tap your brakes like this

00:02:14.017 --> 00:02:16.461
to prevent yourself from falling back.

00:02:16.461 --> 00:02:18.486
I'mma demonstrate it right now.

00:02:19.978 --> 00:02:21.793
You've gotta give yourself some speed.

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:28.520
See how you tap. You tap, tap, tap.

00:02:30.474 --> 00:02:32.532
And that's how you wheelie a bike.

00:02:46.466 --> 00:02:47.938
- [Narrator] You can
catch more of Ferg's moves

00:02:47.938 --> 00:02:49.880
in the "Plain Jane" music video.

00:02:54.423 --> 00:02:56.583
- Haha. A little bit.

00:02:56.583 --> 00:02:58.036
I ain't do that in a long time.

00:02:58.036 --> 00:02:59.940
That was a little scary just now.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:02.531
Woof. I feel 9 again.

00:03:04.365 --> 00:03:05.198
Thank you.

00:03:06.201 --> 00:03:07.384
All right. All right.

